{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-446070-r4513638","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Nigerian Noodles","sourcePageId":446070,"sourceRevision":"4513638","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:07:08Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Nigerian%20Noodles&oldid=4513638","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:29.172Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:National Nigerian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth","Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"bde0857143717225b4e9d32503518f9d324f48492db9ce2d85797c8cd932efe2","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Noodle recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\nNigeria has a variety of packaged noodle brands and numerous ways to prepare them. Brands include Indomie, Golden penny, Minimie, Mimee, Tummy Tummy, etc.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Base ===\n*[[Cookbook:Noodle|Noodles]]\n*[[Cookbook:Bouillon Cube|Seasoning cubes]]\n*Pepper\n*Water\n* Vegetable\n\n=== Optional additions ===\n*[[Cookbook:Egg|Egg]]\n*Roast [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]]\n*Sauce\n*[[Cookbook:Beef|Beef]]\n*[[Cookbook:Onion|Onion]] bulb\n*Green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]]\n*[[Cookbook:Tomato|Tomatoes]]\n*Oil\n\n== Equipment ==\n\n* Pot\n* [[Cookbook:Cooktop|Stove]]\n* [[Cookbook:Knife|Knife]] (optional) \n* Spoon\n* Colander or strainer\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Method I ===\n# Toast the noodles in a dry [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]].\n# Add some [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiling]] water, along with seasoning and pepper.\n# Cook, stirring, until the water is fully absorbed and the noodles are tender.\n# Serve with the optional additions.\n# Use a timer to avoid overcooking\n# Don't overcrowd the pot\n\n=== Method II ===\n#Bring water to a boil in a pot with a dash of oil.\n#Add the noodles, and cook until the noodles are tender.\n#Drain the noodles, and serve with the optional additions.\n\n[[Category:Recipes]]\n[[Category:National Nigerian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Nigerian Noodles","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Noodles","sourceText":"Noodles","amountText":"Noodles","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Seasoning cubes","sourceText":"Seasoning cubes","amountText":"Seasoning cubes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Pepper","sourceText":"Pepper","amountText":"Pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Water","sourceText":"Water","amountText":"Water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Vegetable","sourceText":"Vegetable","amountText":"Vegetable","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Egg","sourceText":"Egg","amountText":"Egg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Roast chicken","sourceText"